WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.034
This query uses CASE to handle several known date
formats Blank strings

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:13.703
become NULL ISO-style text can be cast to date
Slash-formatted

00:00:13.729 --> 00:00:19.256
text uses TO_DATE with a month-day-year pattern
Eight-digit

00:00:19.282 --> 00:00:25.254
text uses a year-month-day pattern Anything else
becomes NULL for review

00:00:26.986 --> 00:00:31.012
The important idea is explicit controlled parsing
rather than guessing
